  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "The Chef shows Maks the real ingredients of the famous pâté. Maks is completely shocked by what he sees. Let us see what happens next in this scene.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Паштет говяжий.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Гадость страшная.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Но если всё смешать...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Ей нравится.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Вы издеваетесь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Почему?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Ты самовоспитывался.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Ну, пойдём.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Кстати, хороший паштет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Как делаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Что добавлял?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Говядина, печень.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's review the scene line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Паштет говяжий.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Beef pâté.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'pâté' straight to 'beef'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Гадость страшная.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Absolutely revolting.' Notice the word order: 'a disgusting thing' comes first, and 'terrible' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Но если всё смешать...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But when you mix it all together...' You'll hear 'mix' all the time in the show, here connected with 'mix'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Ей нравится.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She likes it.' You'll hear 'to her' all the time in the show, here connected with 'is pleasing'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Вы издеваетесь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Are you kidding me?' Maks starts with 'you' and pairs it with 'are you mocking' to make the point clear. And Chef jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Почему?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why?' Chef starts with 'why' and pairs it with 'why' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Ты самовоспитывался.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You were learning to discipline yourself.' Here 'you' sets up the idea, while 'educate oneself' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Ну, пойдём.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, let's go.' In Russian, 'let's go' leads into 'let's go' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Кстати, хороший паштет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'By the way, it's good pâté.' The first content word means 'by the way', and 'pâté' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Как делаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'How do you make it?' A compact expression built around 'how' and 'are you doing'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Что добавлял?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What did you put in?' A compact expression built around 'what' and 'to add'. Then Maks replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Говядина, печень.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Beef, liver.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'beef' straight to 'liver'. Let's listen to the dialog one more time.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
